   },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011wr010608\",\n      \"title\": \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\\nby E Laloy · 2012 · Cited by 663 — In this paper, we present a general framework for efficient inversion of highly parameterized models. This method, entitled MT-DREAM(ZS),\\nHigh‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using ...\\nThis new code is especially designed to solve high-dimensional search problems and receives particularly spectacular performance improvement over other\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://search.sl.nsw.gov.au/primo-explore/fulldisplay?context=PC&docid=TN_cdi_proquest_journals_1020329913&vid=SLNSW\",\n      \"title\": \"High-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing | Catalogue | State Library of New South Wales\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing\\n: Laloy, Eric ; Vrugt, Jasper A. : : Washington: Blackwell Publishing Ltd :\\nWater resources research, 2012-01, Vol.48 (1), p.n/a\\nPEER REVIEWED\\nOPEN ACCESS\\nGet PDF Read Online\\nnui.aria.newWindow High-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing Full text available\\nSend to\\nTitle\\nHigh-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing\\nHigh-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing\\nHigh-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing\\nShow collections Hide collections Show All Show Less\\nAuthor / Creator\\nLaloy, Eric\\nLaloy, Eric\\nLaloy, Eric\\nVrugt, Jasper A.\\nVrugt, Jasper A.\\nVrugt, Jasper A.\\nShow collections Hide collections Show All Show Less\\nContents\\nSpatially distributed hydrologic models are increasingly being used to study and predict soil moisture flow, groundwater recharge, surface runoff, and river discharge.\\nThe usefulness and applicability of such complex models is increasingly held back by the potentially many hundreds (thousands) of parameters that require calibration against some historical record of data.\\nThe current generation of search and optimization algorithms is typically not powerful enough to deal with a very large number of variables and summarize parameter and predictive uncertainty.\\nWe have previously presented a general‐purpose Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithm for Bayesian inference of the posterior probability density function of hydrologic model parameters.\\nThis method, entitled differential evolution adaptive Metropolis (DREAM), runs multiple different Markov chains in parallel and uses a discrete proposal distribution to evolve the sampler to the posterior distribution. The DREAM approach maintains detailed balance and shows excellent performance on complex, multimodal search problems.\\nHere we present our latest algorithmic developments and introduce MT‐DREAM(ZS), which combines the strengths of multiple‐try sampling, snooker updating, and sampling from an archive of past states.\\nThis new code is especially designed to solve high‐dimensional search problems and receives particularly spectacular performance improvement over other adaptive MCMC approaches when using distributed computing. Four different case studies with increasing dimensionality up to 241 parameters are used to illustrate the advantages of MT‐DREAM(ZS).\\nKey Points An efficient MCMC method especially designed to solve high‐dimensional problems A parallelization scheme that maintains detailed balance and ergodicity Multi‐try sampling is admirably suited to treat all sources of error explicitly\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://bg.copernicus.org/preprints/bg-2017-41/bg-2017-41-SC2-supplement.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Microsoft Word - Reponse_SC1.docx\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"On the other hand, Laloy and Vrugt (2012) demonstrated that DREAM can successfully sample the 25-dimensional, three-modal Gaussian function with the two neighboring modes having a separation of 10 units.\\nLaloy, E., and J.A. Vrugt: High-dimensional posterior exploration of hudrologic models using multiply-try DREAM(zs) and high-performance computing, Water resour. Res., 48, W01526, 2012.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://collection.sl.nsw.gov.au/record/TN_cdi_proquest_journals_1020329913\",\n      \"title\": \"High-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing | Collection - State Library of NSW\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-pe...\\nShow all\\nHelp | Ask | Become a Library member\\nHigh-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-pe...\\nShow all\\nhttps://collection.sl.nsw.gov.au/record/TN_cdi_proquest_journals_1020329913\\nHigh-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing\\nAbout this item\\nFull title\\nHigh-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing\\nAuthor / Creator\\nLaloy, Eric and Vrugt, Jasper A.\\nPublisher\\nWashington: Blackwell Publishing Ltd\\nJournal title\\nWater resources research, 2012-01, Vol.48 (1), p.n/a\\nLanguage\\nEnglish\\nFormats\\nArticles\\nPublication information\\nPublisher\\nWashington: Blackwell Publishing Ltd\\nSubjects\\nSubjects and topics\\n* Algorithms\\n* Calibration\\n* DREAM\\n* Efficiency\\n* [Groundwater recharge](/search?search=Groundwater recharge)\\n* [Groundwater runoff](/search?search=Groundwater runoff)\\n* [high parameter dimensionality](/search?search=high parameter dimensionality)\\n* [Hydrologic models](/search?search=Hydrologic models)\\n* Hydrology\\n* [Markov analysis](/search?search=Markov analysis)\\n* [Markov chains](/search?search=Markov chains)\\n* MCMC\\n* Methods\\n* multiple-try\\n* [parallel computing](/search?search=parallel computing)\\n* [River discharge](/search?search=River discharge)\\n* [River flow](/search?search=River flow)\\n* [Soil moisture](/search?search=Soil moisture)\\n* [Surface runoff](/search?search=Surface runoff)\\n* Uncertainty\\nContents\\nSpatially distributed hydrologic models are increasingly being used to study and predict soil moisture flow, groundwater recharge, surface runoff, and river discharge.\\nThe usefulness and applicability of such complex models is increasingly held back by the potentially many hundreds (thousands) of parameters that require calibration against some his...\\nShow more\\nShow More/Show less\\nAlternative Titles\\nFull title\\nHigh-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM(ZS) and high-performance computing\\nAuthors, Artists and Contributors\\nAuthor / Creator\\nLaloy, Eric Vrugt, Jasper A.\\nIdentifiers\\nPrimary Identifiers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://science.uptrusthq.com/paper/7c1d1cf8170b17e368e43831642a289f00686d73\",\n      \"title\": \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using… — Sci-Trust\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Sci-Trust Science corpus · trust-algo showcase\\nBrowse Subfields Compare About\\nBrowse / Paper\\n2012\\nHigh‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM(ZS) and high‐performance computing\\nE Eric Laloy , J Jasper A. Vrugt\\n532 citations\\nView paper →\\nEnvironmental Engineering Global and Planetary Change Water Science and Technology\\nHow researchers see this paper — by subfield\\n…are compared the As no analytical solution of p ( θ | d ) is available for the type of non-linear inverse problems considered herein, we sample from p ( θ | d ) by MCMC simulation (see, e.g., Robert and Casella , 2004) with the DREAM (ZS) algorithm ( Vrugt et al. , 2009; Laloy and Vrugt , 2012).\\nEfficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\\nEric Laloy , B. Rogiers , Jasper A. Vrugt , Dirk Mallants , Diederik Jacques · 2013\\nIn the remainder of this paper, we refer to this approach as strategy A.\\n[41] The state-of-the-art DREAM ZSð Þ [ter Braak and Vrugt, 2008; Vrugt et al., 2009; Laloy and Vrugt, 2012] algorithm is used to generate posterior samples.\\nProbabilistic inference of multi‐Gaussian fields from indirect hydrological data using circulant embedding and dimensionality reduction\\nEric Laloy , Niklas Linde , Diederik Jacques , Jasper A.\\nVrugt · 2015\\n…Gaussian process generation via circulant embedding [Dietrich and Newsam, 1997] to decouple the variogram from grid cell specific values, and implements dimensionality reduction by interpolation to enable MCMC simulation with the DREAM ZSð Þ algorithm [Vrugt et al., 2009; Laloy and Vrugt, 2012].\\nHopmans, Mathieu Javaux , Dani Or , Tiina Roose , J. Vanderborght , M. Young, W. Amelung , M. Aitkenhead , +40 more · 2016\\nRecent developments include multiple try sampling, snooker updates, and sampling from an archive of past states (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012).\\nA global scale mechanistic model of photosynthetic capacity (LUNA V1.0)\\nA. Ali, Chonggang Xu , Alistair Rogers , R. Fisher , S. Wullschleger, E. Massoud, Jasper A. Vrugt , Jordan D. Muss , Nathan G. McDowell , Joshua B. Fisher , +2 more · 2016\\nA detailed description of DREAM(ZS) appears in Vrugt et al.\\n(2008, 2009) and Laloy and Vrugt (2012) and interested readers are referred to these publications for further details.\\nEvaluating marginal likelihood with thermodynamic integration method and comparison with several other numerical methods\\nPeigui Liu , A. Elshall , Ming Ye , Peter Beerli , Xiankui Zeng , Dan Lu , Yuezan Tao · 2016\\nBenchmark experiments in geophysics, hydrology and hydrogeology have shown that this sampler1200 is able to sample correctly high-dimensional target distributions (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012a; Laloy et al., 2012b, 2013; Linde and Vrugt, 2013;1202 Carbajal et al., 2014; Lochbühler et al., 2014, 2015).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://openalex.org/works/W2133944044\",\n      \"title\": \"Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"description: 2013 article in Water Resources Research by Laloy, Rogiers, Vrugt and 2 others; 264 citations; open access title: Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion image: https://openalex.org/brand-assets/openalex-mark-square.png\\nWork\\nAdd to collection\\nEfficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\\nHTML PDF\\nDetailsLocations\\nYear: 2013\\nType: article\\nAbstract: Key Points Efficient two‐stage MCMC simulation for CPU‐demanding sampling Real‐world application to the inference of a multi‐layered 3D aquifer model A 2‐5 times observed speed up in sampling efficiency\\nmore\\nSource: Water Resources Research\\nDOI: 10.1002/wrcr.20226\\nAuthors: Eric Laloy, Bart Rogiers, Jasper A. Vrugt, Dirk Mallants, Diederik Jacques\\nInstitutions: Belgian Nuclear Research Centre, KU Leuven, University of California, Irvine, University of Amsterdam, Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation, CSIRO Land and Water\\nshow all 6\\nLanguage: English\\n{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ScholarlyArticle\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/works/W2133944044\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/works/W2133944044\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos\\nexpansion\\\",\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2013-04-03\\\",\\\"inLanguage\\\":\\\"en\\\",\\\"abstract\\\":\\\"Key Points Efficient two‐stage MCMC simulation for CPU‐demanding sampling Real‐world application to the inference of a multi‐layered 3D aquifer model A 2‐5 times observed speed up in sampling efficiency\\\",\\\"author\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Person\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Eric\\nLaloy\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/authors/A5042170410\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4788-3272\\\"],\\\"affiliation\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Belgian Nuclear Research\\nCentre\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/institutions/I4210114391\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://ror.org/020xs5r81\\\"],\\\"address\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"PostalAddress\\\",\\\"addressCountry\\\":\\\"BE\\\"}}]},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Person\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Bart\\nRogiers\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/authors/A5039395337\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8836-0988\\\"],\\\"affiliation\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Belgian Nuclear Research\\nCentre\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/institutions/I4210114391\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://ror.org/020xs5r81\\\"],\\\"address\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"PostalAddress\\\",\\\"addressCountry\\\":\\\"BE\\\"}},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"KU\\nLeuven\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/institutions/I99464096\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://ror.org/05f950310\\\"],\\\"address\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"PostalAddress\\\",\\\"addressCountry\\\":\\\"BE\\\"}}]},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Person\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Jasper Alexander\\nVrugt\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/authors/A5025871169\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2599-1165\\\"],\\\"affiliation\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"University of California,\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/preprints/gmd-2018-272/gmd-2018-272-AR3.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Bold black font: Topical editor and reviewer comments Black font: Author response Topical Editor Decision: Publish subject to technical corrections\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \", equation (13) becomes the likelihood function corresponding 315\\nto the SLS data model. Replacing 0  t   by 0 1 t t E      , equation (13) becomes the likelihood 316\\nfunction of the WLS data model. 317\\nIn this study, the posterior distributions of the data model parameters are jointly estimated with 318\\nthe soil respiration model parameters using the MT-DREAM(ZS) code (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012). 319\\nMT-DREAM(ZS) implements a Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithm by running 320\\nmultiple Markov chains in parallel with adaptive proposal distribution, multiple-try sampling, and 321\\nsampling from an archive of past states.\\nThese state-of-the-art features assist in overcoming 322\\ncommon challenges in the sampling space such as multimodality, ill-conditioning, and high 323\\ndimensionality, and thus allow for accurate exploration of the targeted distributions. 324\\n2.3 Soil respiration models 325\\nZhang et al.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_ea962aa48ffe7fg2I6fW6DcPEb\"\n}","metadata":{"provider":"parallel","truncated":false},"title":"Parallel Web Search: Laloy Vrugt 2012 high-dimensional posterior exploration hydrologic models multiple-try DREAM(ZS) PDF Nevada Test Site 241 parameters","time":{"start":1792454608070,"end":1792454608889}},"id":"prt_1569ec33f001yeA07vqLVS36GW","sessionID":"ses_ea962aa48ffe7fg2I6fW6DcPEb","messageID":"msg_1569eb2280011jlolNkLgRwlRo"}}
