{"type":"text","timestamp":1792454700375,"sessionID":"ses_ea962aa48ffe7fg2I6fW6DcPEb","part":{"id":"prt_156a01300001jpbt7zAJllnrw7","messageID":"msg_1569f3d58001pGJKpwlRi79abt","sessionID":"ses_ea962aa48ffe7fg2I6fW6DcPEb","type":"text","text":"I have fetched all four source pages. The Wiley page for the Laloy & Vrugt paper returns HTTP 403 (bot-blocked) on both `/full/` and `/abs/`; an alternate PDF copy is binary and not text-extractable, so that quote cannot be verified.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:question\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"We present a new data set of attributes for 671 catchments in the contiguous United States (CONUS) minimally impacted by human activities.\",\n      \"note\": \"Research question the plan will measure; needs no source. The embedded '671 CAMELS catchments' is corroborated by the CAMELS page (also the plan's num:camels_n source).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:hypothesis\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Hypothesis/prediction about GPU batching; no source required. The '671' figure is corroborated by the CAMELS page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:sequential_part\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Plan's own MCMC design settings (100,000 serial proposal-accept steps, 4 chains per catchment); no external factual claim to source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:method\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Method/design statement; 4 chains x 671 catchments = 2,684 chains is internally consistent arithmetic. No external fact to source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:if_lever\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Conditional prediction ('if compute is the lever'); no source required for what the plan predicts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:if_not\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Conditional prediction ('if compute is not the lever'); no source required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:test_summary\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Test/measurement plan (4 chains x 1e5 iterations, R-hat<1.2); no source required for what the plan will measure. '671 CAMELS catchments' corroborated by the CAMELS page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:closest_prior\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\",\n      \"note\": \"Quote appears verbatim. Page (Freitas, Mendes, Ilic 2022) is on the MGB hydrological model and MOCOM-UA (Multi-Objective Complex Evolution) calibration for two watersheds — a distributed model with an evolutionary optimizer, i.e. not batched MCMC across GR4J catchments. Supports '20x CPU speedup for calibration on one distributed model'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:left_open\",\n      \"status\": \"UNSUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\",\n      \"note\": \"The cited source (s_mgb) describes a single paper (MGB + MOCOM-UA, 20x CPU). It cannot establish the universal negative claim that 'no published result times batched GPU MCMC on all 671 CAMELS catchments'; a single paper's difference is not evidence of absence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:anchor\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"The parameter set corresponding to the best criterion is the following: X1 X2 X3 X4 = 165.05 6.46 422.50 2.45 ... The Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency criterion computed on the calibration period is better (0.495) than with the generalist parameter sets.\",\n      \"note\": \"Page shows GR4J parameter set (165.05, 6.46, 422.50, 2.45) giving calibration NSE 0.495. Value 0.495 matches the page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:limits\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Scope/limits statement (GR4J only, US CAMELS, no single-chain mixing analysis); no external factual claim requiring a source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"src:s_airgr_nse\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"The Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency criterion computed on the calibration period is better (0.495) than with the generalist parameter sets, but the one computed on the validation period is lower (0.57).\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim (as the leading clause). Supports anchor_nse = 0.495.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"src:s_mgb\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim in the abstract. Supports speedup_threshold = 20 (PROXY) for the calibration case.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"num:camels_n\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"We present a new data set of attributes for 671 catchments in the contiguous United States (CONUS) minimally impacted by human activities.\",\n      \"note\": \"Recorded quote appears verbatim; page states 671 catchments.\",\n      \"page_value\": 671\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"num:dist_evals_per_catchment\",\n      \"status\": \"UNREACHABLE\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Source URL (agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011WR010608) returns HTTP 403 on both /full/ and /abs/; page could not be fetched to confirm the '50 million surrogate model evaluations' quote. An alternate PDF copy of the paper is binary and not text-extractable via the fetch tool.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","time":{"start":1792454693632,"end":1792454700365}}}
